      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHISKEY WARRIOR (5) comes off a Toowoomba second as favourite and has placed at this distance. Heading the right way on the quick back-up and has more upside than others. JOSEPHINE OF TUFFY (2) has become quite the bridesmaid but is still desperate to break through. Expect her to hunt the front again and be the one they need to reel in when they straighten. FIVE OF US (3) finds the maiden win elusive but is knocking on the door, backing up a narrow Eagle Farm second with another close finish at this track when sent favourite last time. Shoulders a good record here and Larson sticks. Bold showing anticipated. CHANCE DE LUNE (8) is harder to trust as a 17-start maiden without a placing, but suspect the rise in trip is what he's been calling for. DESERT ANGEL (6) was plain last start, though her long-neck second at this venue two back is strong enough to put her in the mix if repeated.",
